        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Krea 2 Raw with LoRAs\n\n**Raw** is the undistilled Krea 2 base: the checkpoint LoRAs and fine-tunes are trained on, with the widest variety\nand a real negative prompt. It is much slower than Turbo (`krea2_turbo_fp8_scaled.safetensors`, 8 steps).\n\n**Settings**: about 52 steps, CFG 3.5 (true CFG: two passes per step), 1024×1024 (up to 2048×2048). Krea gives no\nsampler or scheduler for Raw: euler / simple are a starting point. The negative prompt works at CFG 3.5; keep it short\nor leave it empty.\n\n**Prompts**: full descriptive sentences (subject, setting, composition, lighting, materials, mood), not tag\nlists. Stay well under ~500 tokens: very long prompts produce black images. `(word:1.2)` weights are not\nknown to work.\n\n## Image Bench\n\n| Marker | Node | Generate tab |\n|--------|------|--------------|\n| `ib:cp` | Load Diffusion Model | model list, model exploration |\n| `ib:pp` / `ib:np` | Image Bench Prompt / Negative Prompt | prompts and LoRA list |\n| `ib:smp` | KSampler | seed, steps, CFG scale, sampling method, schedule type |\n| `ib:lora` | Load LoRA (bypassed) | LoRA exploration only |\n\n**LoRAs**: check them in the LoRA list of the Generate tab, or type `<lora:name:weight>` into the prompt; the **Image\nBench Prompt** node applies them. **Load LoRA** stays bypassed; LoRA exploration enables it for its runs and bypasses\nit again.\n\n**Style LoRAs** ([Comfy-Org/Krea-2/loras](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/tree/main/loras), strength 1.0) need\ntheir trigger words in the prompt, e.g. `<lora:krea2_darkbrush:1> monochrome ink wash style` (`darkbrush`: monochrome\nink wash style, `dotmatrix`: monochrome stippling style, `kidsdrawing`: naive expressive sketch style, `neondrip`:\ntextured abstract style, `rainywindow`: rainy window style, `retroanime`: purple retro anime style, `softwatercolor`:\nart deco watercolor style, `sunsetblur`: ethereal motion blur style, `vintagetarot`: vintage tarot style).\n\nThe size is that of **Empty Latent Image**.\n\n## Model Links\n\n[Comfy-Org/Krea-2](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2) also has `*_bf16` and `*_int8_convrot` diffusion models of\nRaw and Turbo, `krea2_turbo_mxfp8` / `krea2_turbo_nvfp4` (RTX 50), and the bf16 / int8 text encoders.\n\n**diffusion_models**: [krea2_raw_fp8_scaled.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/diffusion_models/krea2_raw_fp8_scaled.safetensors), [krea2_turbo_fp8_scaled.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/diffusion_models/krea2_turbo_fp8_scaled.safetensors)\n**text_encoders**: [qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/text_encoders/qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors) (one file for Raw and Turbo)\n**vae**: [qwen_image_vae.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/vae/qwen_image_vae.safetensors) (the Qwen-Image VAE)\n**loras**: [krea2_darkbrush.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/loras/krea2_darkbrush.safetensors)\n\nKrea 2 is released under the Krea 2 Community License.\n"
      ],
